{"data": [{"author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-10-29T12:31:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115783702537990558"], "id": "2115783702537990558", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1749, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "People’s incomes rose 0.2% in September; spending grew 0.5%. Both figures are in current dollars. \n \nhttps://t.co/eDZgP9dcXM", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2115783702537990558"}, {"author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-10-29T12:30:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115783405661020555"], "id": "2115783405661020555", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2364, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "The U.S. economy grew at a 3.4% annualized rate in Q3.  \n \nhttps://t.co/qHGf5n47pp \n \n#GDP", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2115783405661020555"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-29T11:30:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115768147873796106"], "id": "2115768147873796106", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 20892, "like_count": 118, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 41}, "text": "Tax cuts in major economies can reduce output elsewhere, as the effects of capital reallocation can outweigh the benefits from stronger import demand. See our new blog. https://t.co/B4Ryew065W https://t.co/0RuaLpG1rW", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2115768147873796106"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:00:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115745578487292038"], "id": "2115745578487292038", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 83, "impression_count": 94988, "like_count": 728, "quote_count": 74, "reply_count": 176, "retweet_count": 238}, "text": "President Lagarde has informed the Governing Council and the President of the European Council António Costa that she will step down from her position on 7 February 2027.\n\nHer successor will be appointed by the European Council in due course.\n\nPress release https://t.co/qHD6JvIppk", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2115745578487292038"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:00:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115745464590954925"], "id": "2115745464590954925", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 61, "impression_count": 114892, "like_count": 496, "quote_count": 23, "reply_count": 43, "retweet_count": 108}, "text": "Economists who map the CPI and PPI into the PCE expect core prices to have increased 0.34% in September (4.2% annualized, 3.1% year-over year)\n\nThis would be the highest monthly reading since January's 0.40% core PCE print https://t.co/qCNeyqSHU7", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2115745464590954925"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115745462514823204"], "id": "2115745462514823204", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 10847, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "Later today: watch live as ECB President Christine @Lagarde explains the latest monetary policy decisions https://t.co/zk696aG3mL https://t.co/OsiMxEfNMq", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2115745462514823204"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-29T09:36:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115739589013069931"], "id": "2115739589013069931", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 11161, "like_count": 149, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 26}, "text": "🇪🇸🇪🇺 We are deeply saddened by the tragic train accident in Urda.\n\nWe extend our deepest sympathies to the victims, their families and the people of Spain.\n\nTogether with other EU institutions, we are flying our flags at half-mast in remembrance.\n\nEuropa llora con vosotros. https://t.co/ozkyMcvpES", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2115739589013069931"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-10-29T09:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115737907290157360"], "id": "2115737907290157360", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 46, "impression_count": 86590, "like_count": 319, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 25, "retweet_count": 50}, "text": "For months, a common view has been that the AI boom is carrying the U.S. economy and that it is too flush with cash and too big to care much about interest rates.\n\nKevin Warsh pushed back against both framings on Wednesday. \"Interest rates get in the cracks,\" he said, and growth", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2115737907290157360"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-29T04:57:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115669223595000284"], "id": "2115669223595000284", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2268, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Carbon, Carbon my man https://t.co/LHcb3XZC59", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115669223595000284"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-29T02:59:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115639571270812064"], "id": "2115639571270812064", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 171, "impression_count": 137189, "like_count": 935, "quote_count": 50, "reply_count": 35, "retweet_count": 103}, "text": "If you believe that mindless AI evaluations are legitimate then why would you spread the evaluation of Saez &amp; @gabriel_zucman without first subjecting it to its own mindless AI evaluation?\n\nI just did and it turns out the critic's errors all go in one direction. https://t.co/7ZnHnrx8lZ", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115639571270812064"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-29T01:55:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115623596530012464"], "id": "2115623596530012464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2773, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115562063431078370", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Yeppers https://t.co/suBDsh0O6d", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115623596530012464"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-29T01:54:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115623195319644435"], "id": "2115623195319644435", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3057, "like_count": 62, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115412659763916912", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "https://t.co/OqOcdNuZmX https://t.co/KRDaHcIX8U", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115623195319644435"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-29T00:00:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115594672471195779"], "id": "2115594672471195779", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 100, "impression_count": 35824, "like_count": 420, "quote_count": 22, "reply_count": 185, "retweet_count": 42}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115519456491511996", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Academics have to invest tremendous effort into a single paper, so we often work on papers that we suspect will yield interesting &amp; significant results. But that also pushes us to predictable work.\n\nAI has no such constraints, forcing us to rethink a lot of how science is done. https://t.co/ty1Zlec9mM", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115594672471195779"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-28T23:20:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115584471089262988"], "id": "2115584471089262988", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 21092, "like_count": 455, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 58, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "I just found out that my new book, Co-Existence, debuted at #3 on the New York Times bestseller list. Thank you so much to everyone who bought a copy! https://t.co/SgSCVnMWnt", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115584471089262988"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-28T23:20:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115584395494961631"], "id": "2115584395494961631", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2689, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Haul-o-ween: sugar and confectionery products manufacturing https://t.co/YWxCl5qxgu #BLSdata https://t.co/Y4xuG3tzhz", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2115584395494961631"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T23:08:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115581593314337181"], "id": "2115581593314337181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3380, "like_count": 85, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Are we entering the Carbon-era? https://t.co/uoLykjOuZP", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115581593314337181"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:33:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115557598107746657"], "id": "2115557598107746657", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 75, "impression_count": 110159, "like_count": 445, "quote_count": 19, "reply_count": 70, "retweet_count": 74}, "text": "The key question ahead of the Fed meeting today was if economic activity is strengthening and broadening, inflation remains elevated, and most people think rates need to go up again, why wait until December?\n\nHere's how Fed Chairman Kevin Warsh asked the question (put to him by https://t.co/FG98HBCaAd", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2115557598107746657"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:13:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115552548438315297"], "id": "2115552548438315297", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 9174, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Big data day tomorrow. First look at GDP for Q3--Econvitals Composite is reading 3.2%.\n\nAnd PCE inflation for September. Econvitals tracking:\n\nPCE: 0.51% MoM / 3.6% YoY\nCore PCE: 0.32% MoM / 3.1% YoY https://t.co/nC1dfLdlQb", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115552548438315297"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "321536046", "name": "BEA News", "username": "BEA_News"}, {"id": "25098482", "name": "IMF", "username": "IMFNews"}, {"id": "83466368", "name": "European Central Bank", "username": "ecb"}, {"id": "59603406", "name": "Nick Timiraos", "username": "NickTimiraos"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2115783702537990558", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlxo4j0gg3s96mrh5byec26o4fb1", "oldest_id": "2115552548438315297", "result_count": 18}}
